index ea1a1a0..138e89e 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,36 @@ Semantic Versioning.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Add `v1` `Files.Upload`, which takes a file name and an `io.Reader` and
+  encodes the `multipart/form-data` body itself, with options for the record
+  associations the endpoint accepts (`WithFileDealID`, `WithFilePersonID`,
+  `WithFileOrganizationID`, `WithFileProductID`, `WithFileActivityID`,
+  `WithFileProjectID`, `WithFileLeadID`) and `WithFileFormField` for anything
+  not wrapped yet. `Files.Add` still accepts a pre-encoded body.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Retries now apply to requests whose body is a seekable `io.Reader`, such as
+  an upload streamed from `os.Open`. `net/http` only derives `GetBody` from
+  `*bytes.Buffer`, `*bytes.Reader` and `*strings.Reader`, so these requests
+  reached the retry transport as non-replayable and were never retried -- not
+  even on 429, and regardless of `RetryPolicy.RetryAllMethods`. This affected
+  `v1` `Files.Add` and `Files.Update`; JSON and form-encoded calls were
+  unaffected. Such requests now also send a `Content-Length` instead of using
+  chunked encoding.
+
+### Changed
+
+- `v1` `WithFilesQuery` and `WithFilesRequestOptions` now return
+  `FilesRequestOption` so they also apply to `Files.Upload`. Both still satisfy
+  `FilesOption`, so existing calls are unaffected.
+- A seekable `io.Reader` passed as a request body is no longer closed by the
+  transport, since it has to stay readable across retry attempts. Closing it
+  remains the caller's responsibility, as it already was for every other
+  reader type.
+
 ## [1.11.0] - 2026-08-18
 
 ### Added
